- id: D261108-fyhht
  timestamp: 2026-11-08T09:28:22Z
  actor: user
  status: active
  approved_by:
    name: Anton Solo
    email: anton@50lo.me
    at: 2026-11-08T10:44:43Z
  summary: 'Adopt six core analysis rules: a change is measured from the merge-base, analysis never writes into the reviewed repo, name-matched references always carry a warning, a failed LLM reply keeps the deterministic report, every finding is anchored to something on the map, and formatting-only changes ask for no review.'
  rationale: 'These are the guarantees a reviewer relies on when reading a map, and all six already hold in the code, so writing them down records current behavior and lets statute flag changes that would break them. Rejected for now: per-branch reviewed marks (viewer convenience, not core), refusing reports older than version 4 (no enforcing code found), and byte-identical reports for the same inputs (not verified; warnings are stored in a set). CORE-003 deliberately puts the guarantee on the per-language warnings rather than analyzer.resolution, which reads index when any language was indexed.'
  establishes:
  - CORE-001
  - CORE-002
  - CORE-003
  - CORE-004
  - CORE-005
  - CORE-006
  changes: []
  retires: []
  terms: []
- id: D261115-bbchl
  timestamp: 2026-11-15T11:33:30Z
  actor: user
  status: active
  approved_by:
    name: Anton Solo
    email: anton@50lo.me
    at: 2026-11-15T20:30:15Z
  summary: 'Change CORE-003: the main change report never matches references by name. A language without a usable index (the build failed, indexing was cancelled, or indexes are off), and every file an index misses, stays syntax-only with a warning that names the language and the reason. unused-api, orphaned and untested run only when the index covers every file that could hold the reference. Name matching stays in the labelled comparison report.'
  rationale: 'The user''s goal is that everything the review shows is true. Name matching produced the false positives that made index mode the prototype''s default, and as a fallback it showed those links again exactly when the index failed. Chosen by the user on 2026-11-15: syntax-only also for partial indexes and with indexes turned off, and the checks held back unless coverage is complete, accepting that untested rarely runs when test targets are outside the review scope and that an uncovered file anywhere holds the checks back. Rejected: keeping name matching for uncovered files; letting the absence of a name in uncovered files stand in for coverage, which misses implicit uses such as operators and delegates. The comparison report stays because the rebuild proposal asks for indexed and non-indexed results side by side during validation. The prototype (Sources/) keeps the old behaviour as the comparison baseline, so its CORE-003 links are removed. Conformers and overrides still resolve supertype names from inheritance clauses in indexed languages; that is recorded as a gap, and they are held back for syntax-only languages.'
  establishes: []
  changes:
  - CORE-003
  retires: []
  terms: []
